2. MXFP4 x FP8 GEMM design, derived  -- NOT Apache-2.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    kernels/r9k_moe_mxfp4a8.hip       (in part)
    kernels/r9k_gemm_fp8.hip          (in part)
    r9700_vllm/kernels/moe.py         (the weight layout, ~lines 100-109)

    These derive from libr4d by StillDeadcode
    (https://codeberg.org/StillDeadcode/libr4d, commit 5dc6302): the
    fragment-order weight layout, the folded e2m1 -> e4m3 unpack with its kMag
    permute table, and the in-block split-K structure. Most of each file is
    original work -- see notes/independence.md for a line-level accounting --
    but the lineage is real.

    libr4d ships no licence file. The author confirmed by DM on 2026-09-21 that
    our use is fine. That is permission for this project; it is NOT a licence,
    and it is NOT sublicensed under Apache-2.0. If you want to reuse these
    parts, ask StillDeadcode.

